failure_location.quote:
From standard definition of local truncation error, there exist $h_{local}, C_{local} > 0$ such that $\forall h \in (0, h_{local}]$, $\forall x_k \in V^{-1}([0, \varepsilon])$, $x_{k+1}$ remains within $V^{-1}([0, c])$ and 

	\begin{equation}
		e \coloneqq | x_{k+1} - x(h;x_k) | \leq C_{local} h^{p+1},
	\end{equation}
